### 2. GitHub Actions CI Workflow

#### [NEW] [.github/workflows/r-check.yml](file:///h:/omicsflow_test/.github/workflows/r-check.yml)
A lightweight CI pipeline that will trigger on pushes and pull requests to `main` and `feature/*` branches.
- Uses `r-lib/actions/setup-r` and `setup-r-dependencies`.
- Installs the package via `remotes::install_local()`.
- Runs a smoke test script:
  - `library(OmicsFlow)`
  - `generate_metadata_templates(rna = "data/synthetic/rna.rds")`
  - `validate_inputs(rna = "data/...", meth = "data/...")`
  - Verifies exported API structure using `stopifnot()`.
  
*Note: No MOFA+ or heavy ML execution in CI to maintain fast runner times and lightweight test stability.*

